# Two errors inside one string are reported in source order.
mode: syntax
---- query
t | where s == '\q\u{zz}'
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..26
  PIPELINE@0..25
    NAME_REF@0..1
      IDENT@0..1 "t"
    WHITESPACE@1..2 " "
    PIPE@2..3 "|"
    WHITESPACE@3..4 " "
    WHERE_OP@4..25
      IDENT@4..9 "where"
      WHITESPACE@9..10 " "
      BIN_EXPR@10..25
        NAME_REF@10..11
          IDENT@10..11 "s"
        WHITESPACE@11..12 " "
        EQ2@12..14 "=="
        WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
        LITERAL@15..25
          STRING@15..25 "'\\q\\u{zz}'"
  WHITESPACE@25..26 "\n"

error[DS0005]: unknown escape sequence `\q`
  --> query:1:17
  |
1 | t | where s == '\q\u{zz}'
  |                 ^^ not a valid escape
  |
  = help: to write a backslash, double it: `'\\q\u{zz}'`
  = note: valid escapes are `\\`, `\"`, `\'`, `\n`, `\r`, `\t`, `\0` and `\u{...}`

error[DS0005]: invalid unicode escape `\u{zz}`
  --> query:1:19
  |
1 | t | where s == '\q\u{zz}'
  |                   ^^^^^^ not a valid unicode escape
  |
  = help: write `\u{` followed by 1 to 6 hex digits and `}`, e.g. `\u{1F600}`
